# Fleet celld.env — agreed non-default tuning for bucket/fleet nodes.
# NOT used by local `celld dev` (dev runs one node with a local store).
# Source of truth for names/defaults: docs/README.md in the celld clone
# (denoland/celld) plus `celld -h`. If this file disagrees with those, follow them.
#
# Tradeoffs (why these are slower/lazier than defaults):
# - Slower failover: CELLD_TTL_MS=360000 stretches lease expiry/renewal, so a
#   dead node keeps its cells ~6 min before others take over (vs ~10 s).
# - Lazier placement: CELLD_REBALANCE_INTERVAL_MS=300000 samples the fleet
#   every 5 min (vs 5 s), so idle cells converge slowly; 0 would disable it.
# - Later deploys: CELLD_DEPLOY_POLL_S=300 checks deploy/current.json every
#   5 min (vs 30 s); use POST /reload on the internal listener for immediacy.
# - Later alarms: CELLD_WAKER_TICK_MS=600000 scans orphan/due alarms every
#   10 min (vs 60 s), so crashed-session wakeups and cleanups lag.
# - Bounded history at a GC cost: CELLD_LTX_RETENTION_SECS=604800 (7 days)
#   lets owners delete superseded epochs; unset (default) keeps them forever.
# - Smaller memory footprint, more cold starts: CELLD_IDLE_EVICT_S=180
#   hibernates idle cells after 3 min; unset (default) keeps them resident
#   until pressure or the residency cap.
# - Fixed memory ceiling: CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB=6400 sheds under pressure at
#   6.4 GB; default is 80% of available memory.
# - Hard residency cap: CELLD_MAX_RESIDENT_CELLS=500 refuses new activations
#   past 500 residents; default is unset (no cap).
# Do NOT set CELLD_EVICTIONS — removed; the node refuses to boot on it
# (see docs/README.md "These settings are removed").

CELLD_TTL_MS=360000                  # default 10000; lease renews at TTL/3 => ~120s
CELLD_REBALANCE_INTERVAL_MS=300000   # default 5000; 0 disables balancing
CELLD_DEPLOY_POLL_S=300              # default 30; POST /reload on the internal port for immediacy
CELLD_WAKER_TICK_MS=600000           # default 60000
CELLD_LTX_RETENTION_SECS=604800      # default unset => LTX history grows forever; 7 days
CELLD_IDLE_EVICT_S=180               # default unset => cells stay resident
CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB=6400                # default 80% of available memory
CELLD_MAX_RESIDENT_CELLS=500         # default unset
